01:45:29.970 --> 01:45:31.636
Why?
- It is literally all bone.

01:45:31.636 --> 01:45:32.610
- [Joey] Oh my God.

01:45:32.610 --> 01:45:33.750
What the fuck?

01:45:33.750 --> 01:45:36.240
That looks like a dark souls dungeon.

01:45:36.240 --> 01:45:38.460
- [Garnt] That (laughs) is literally

01:45:38.460 --> 01:45:39.967
where the final boss lays.

01:45:39.967 --> 01:45:41.160
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

01:45:41.160 --> 01:45:42.240
- That's fucking horrific.

01:45:42.240 --> 01:45:44.250
- [Garnt] That's the end
game in Elden Ring, man.

01:45:44.250 --> 01:45:45.411
Jesus Christ.

01:45:45.411 --> 01:45:46.830
- I didn't imagine the skulls
being a part of the equation.

01:45:46.830 --> 01:45:48.750
I thought it was just like
bones, tibias and shit.

01:45:48.750 --> 01:45:50.370
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:45:50.370 --> 01:45:51.330
Fucking hell.

01:45:51.330 --> 01:45:54.390
- Like so, you would
happily move into a house

01:45:54.390 --> 01:45:56.160
where someone got murdered?

01:45:56.160 --> 01:45:57.330
- Oh God, yeah.

01:45:57.330 --> 01:45:58.650
- [Garnt] Really?

01:45:58.650 --> 01:46:00.370
- If I'm getting a deal on this. Yeah.

01:46:00.370 --> 01:46:01.203
- [Joey] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:46:01.203 --> 01:46:02.700
- I'll be at the fucking meeting with them

01:46:02.700 --> 01:46:06.600
being like, "Oh, I dunno,
10% off is a little.

01:46:06.600 --> 01:46:08.640
Ooh, someone did die?

01:46:08.640 --> 01:46:12.150
Maybe 15, 20% off?" (inhaling)

01:46:12.150 --> 01:46:13.890
- How low would you be willing to go?

01:46:13.890 --> 01:46:15.450
Like how much would you negotiate down

01:46:15.450 --> 01:46:16.950
if you knew someone
had died in this house?

01:46:16.950 --> 01:46:18.700
- I'd try at least get a third off.

01:46:19.617 --> 01:46:21.150
- 'Cause like that's
actually a pretty big thing

01:46:21.150 --> 01:46:22.230
in Japan, isn't it?

01:46:22.230 --> 01:46:23.730
Not people getting brutally murdered,

01:46:23.730 --> 01:46:28.650
but like houses where people
have died of natural causes.

01:46:28.650 --> 01:46:31.230
- Listen, Garnt, in this
market, you can't be picky.

01:46:31.230 --> 01:46:33.220
You gotta take what you
can get if it's a steal.

01:46:33.220 --> 01:46:34.350
- [Garnt] That is true.
That is true. That is true.

01:46:34.350 --> 01:46:35.610
- I'll be like, "Who died in here?

01:46:35.610 --> 01:46:36.443
Oh, yeah? Great. Yeah, yeah.

01:46:36.443 --> 01:46:38.010
I'm moving in now, is that all right?"

01:46:38.010 --> 01:46:40.529
- There's a website actually.
- [Connor] I know, yeah, yeah.

01:46:40.529 --> 01:46:41.362
- Which is like a real estate website

01:46:41.362 --> 01:46:43.950
where it tells you which
houses are on sale of like,

01:46:43.950 --> 01:46:48.000
they call it jiko bukken or
like accident apartments,

01:46:48.000 --> 01:46:49.780
where some horrible

01:46:51.000 --> 01:46:52.860
accident has happened
and now it's on sale.

01:46:52.860 --> 01:46:54.840
- Why would that affect
your view of the apartment

01:46:54.840 --> 01:46:55.840
or the house though?

01:46:57.516 --> 01:46:58.349
It's like saying,

01:46:58.349 --> 01:47:00.030
oh, if someone had used
that swing and died on it,

01:47:00.030 --> 01:47:01.712
would you not want to use it?

01:47:01.712 --> 01:47:02.545
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:47:02.545 --> 01:47:03.840
- Well, probably not.

01:47:03.840 --> 01:47:05.760
- Is it because they lived there?

01:47:05.760 --> 01:47:08.688
Is that what like adds the weight to it?

01:47:08.688 --> 01:47:09.800
To me, I don't quite-

01:47:09.800 --> 01:47:12.775
- To me, like a house is
just personal, you know?

01:47:12.775 --> 01:47:14.844
It's like your personal space.

01:47:14.844 --> 01:47:16.620
- It's not a house. It's a home. (laughs)

01:47:16.620 --> 01:47:17.970
- That's true. That's true.

01:47:19.410 --> 01:47:21.417
- To me, it's like, what
makes a home is the, you know,

01:47:21.417 --> 01:47:23.970
the way that you've made it yours, right?

01:47:23.970 --> 01:47:27.750
It's like the base walls and
floors don't mean shit to me,

01:47:27.750 --> 01:47:29.460
but all my stuff, that's my couch,

01:47:29.460 --> 01:47:31.440
that's my TV and I put it there.

01:47:31.440 --> 01:47:35.040
That's what makes it me,
well, to me at least.

01:47:35.040 --> 01:47:37.920
So, when you know, that's why
when I move into an apartment,

01:47:37.920 --> 01:47:38.753
I'm like, "Oh, it's weird.

01:47:38.753 --> 01:47:39.780
Someone used to live here."

01:47:39.780 --> 01:47:40.950
I'm like, "Oh, it's a box."

01:47:40.950 --> 01:47:41.783
- No, no.

01:47:41.783 --> 01:47:43.256
I don't think that of like,
someone used to live here,

01:47:43.256 --> 01:47:44.370
but like, there's a big
difference between, oh,

01:47:44.370 --> 01:47:46.503
someone lived here for 30 years and, oh,

01:47:47.640 --> 01:47:50.730
that guy was dead there
a couple years ago.

01:47:50.730 --> 01:47:54.030
Like brutally, I'm not okay with that.

01:47:54.030 --> 01:47:54.863
- Yeah. I know, it's-

01:47:54.863 --> 01:47:56.575
- But if it's not there anymore,

01:47:56.575 --> 01:47:58.980
it's not like you moving in and it's like,

01:47:58.980 --> 01:48:00.660
don't mind the dead guy,
he's been there for a while.

01:48:00.660 --> 01:48:01.951
- Step over him real quick.

01:48:01.951 --> 01:48:03.810
- (cross-talking) insurance
should get rid of it. Oh.

01:48:03.810 --> 01:48:04.710
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:48:04.710 --> 01:48:05.610
- Well, it's like, you know,

01:48:05.610 --> 01:48:07.956
having your, what was it like?

01:48:07.956 --> 01:48:10.680
I guess, it goes back into
partly into like superstition.

01:48:10.680 --> 01:48:12.900
- I think it's a how, you know,

01:48:12.900 --> 01:48:15.267
I'm not religious, I'm not
very spiritual or anything.

01:48:15.267 --> 01:48:18.930
So, I don't have any sort
of connection with death

01:48:18.930 --> 01:48:20.817
and people or anything.

01:48:20.817 --> 01:48:23.160
I just think it's a steal.

01:48:23.160 --> 01:48:24.180
- You just think it's a building.

01:48:24.180 --> 01:48:25.446
- It's free real estate.

01:48:25.446 --> 01:48:26.279
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:48:26.279 --> 01:48:27.120
- Literally. Literally, right? Right?

01:48:27.120 --> 01:48:28.675
- Free real estate.

01:48:28.675 --> 01:48:29.527
- Literally free real estate.

01:48:29.527 --> 01:48:32.110
(all laughing)

01:48:33.300 --> 01:48:35.340
Originally, like sometimes
when houses were really cheap

01:48:35.340 --> 01:48:36.773
in Japan here, I would
go and look, so I'm like,

01:48:36.773 --> 01:48:38.950
there's no way this is this cheap.

01:48:38.950 --> 01:48:39.783
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:48:39.783 --> 01:48:41.040
- And then you'd go online you would see,

01:48:41.040 --> 01:48:43.530
occasionally, that actually
someone had passed in there.

01:48:43.530 --> 01:48:44.598
- [Joey] Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:48:44.598 --> 01:48:45.431
- But you know,

01:48:45.431 --> 01:48:47.430
if there's so many apartments where like,

01:48:48.510 --> 01:48:50.640
eventually everyone has
to die in an apartment.

01:48:50.640 --> 01:48:51.630
- Yeah.

01:48:51.630 --> 01:48:53.540
- Or somewhere.
- Or somewhere, yeah.

01:48:53.540 --> 01:48:54.570
- Or somewhere, yes.

01:48:54.570 --> 01:48:57.240
- But it's also like, that's like,

01:48:57.240 --> 01:48:59.220
what if something like a battle

01:48:59.220 --> 01:49:01.680
or something happened on a piece of land,

01:49:01.680 --> 01:49:03.927
does that affect if you
built something on it?

01:49:03.927 --> 01:49:05.160
- Uh.
- What about it?

01:49:05.160 --> 01:49:06.480
Is it 'cause it's just a personal feeling

01:49:06.480 --> 01:49:07.380
like it's 'cause it's a house?

01:49:07.380 --> 01:49:08.430
I'm trying to get like,

01:49:08.430 --> 01:49:10.440
because like in Ikebukuro, right?

01:49:10.440 --> 01:49:11.273
There's

01:49:12.390 --> 01:49:13.470
Sunshine City.

01:49:13.470 --> 01:49:15.180
- [Garnt And Joey] Yeah.

01:49:15.180 --> 01:49:18.750
That was built on like
a POW camp originally.

01:49:18.750 --> 01:49:19.583
- Was it actually?
- Yeah.

01:49:19.583 --> 01:49:20.416
- I didn't know that.

01:49:20.416 --> 01:49:21.510
- That's why they called it Sunshine.

01:49:21.510 --> 01:49:23.010
Because they were like let's rebrand it

01:49:23.010 --> 01:49:24.270
to make it more happy.

01:49:24.270 --> 01:49:26.430
- Well, they weren't gonna
call it... (laughing)

01:49:26.430 --> 01:49:28.885
- Prisoner of War prison.
- Prisoner of War City.

01:49:28.885 --> 01:49:29.882
POW City.

01:49:29.882 --> 01:49:30.715
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:49:30.715 --> 01:49:33.540
- Yeah, like I think
it was like one of the,

01:49:33.540 --> 01:49:35.177
that's why they renamed
it to be like Sunshine

01:49:35.177 --> 01:49:36.780
'cause they wanted it to be more positive.

01:49:36.780 --> 01:49:37.985
- [Joey] Really?

01:49:37.985 --> 01:49:38.818
- If you, I believe, can you check this?

01:49:38.818 --> 01:49:39.690
- Holy shit, I did not know that.

01:49:39.690 --> 01:49:40.523
- I believe, yeah.

01:49:40.523 --> 01:49:42.357
I believe that it was a
prisoner of war camp before.

01:49:42.357 --> 01:49:44.460
And so you'd think like, I don't go there

01:49:44.460 --> 01:49:46.020
and I'm like, "Oh fuck, man. Oh, Jesus."

01:49:46.020 --> 01:49:48.300
- I think for me it's more
so about like the recency

01:49:48.300 --> 01:49:49.133
of the event, right?

01:49:49.133 --> 01:49:50.793
Like 'cause-
- That's fair enough.

01:49:50.793 --> 01:49:51.626
- You know-

01:49:51.626 --> 01:49:53.760
- So, it's a mixture between
recency plus intimacy.

01:49:53.760 --> 01:49:54.990
- Yeah. Recency and intimacy.

01:49:54.990 --> 01:49:57.390
Like, you know, I'm sure
there's a ton of land

01:49:57.390 --> 01:49:58.510
all around us that was, you know,

01:49:58.510 --> 01:50:00.180
where probably soldiers and, you know,

01:50:00.180 --> 01:50:01.080
people just died, right?

01:50:01.080 --> 01:50:03.480
But it's like, that
happened a very, very, very

01:50:03.480 --> 01:50:04.313
long time ago.

01:50:04.313 --> 01:50:05.550
Whereas if someone, you know,

01:50:05.550 --> 01:50:08.430
just last year got brutally
murdered in this living room

01:50:08.430 --> 01:50:09.810
then, yeah, I'd be a
little more uncomfortable.

01:50:09.810 --> 01:50:11.520
- It's just not a nice thought

01:50:11.520 --> 01:50:13.980
knowing that, I guess,
such an atrocious thing

01:50:13.980 --> 01:50:16.256
happened in the very spot that you're-

01:50:16.256 --> 01:50:17.130
- Are we talking about
just murder, by the way?

01:50:17.130 --> 01:50:20.010
- Yeah. Well, just if someone
died from natural causes,

01:50:20.010 --> 01:50:21.060
I'm okay with that.

01:50:21.060 --> 01:50:22.840
- My concern would be with
murder or something, right?

01:50:22.840 --> 01:50:25.290
It's like, all right, what
if the guy got murdered?

01:50:25.290 --> 01:50:27.900
He was involved in like gangs
or something, dealing, right?

01:50:27.900 --> 01:50:30.390
I don't want, on their address book,

01:50:30.390 --> 01:50:32.910
for it to be like the guy
that we hate lives here.

01:50:32.910 --> 01:50:34.140
- [Joey] Yeah. (laughs)

01:50:34.140 --> 01:50:35.340
And then they come to my-

01:50:35.340 --> 01:50:36.173
- [Joey] Knock knock.

01:50:36.173 --> 01:50:38.430
- Yeah. I would probably be
asking a bit more questions.

01:50:38.430 --> 01:50:39.600
'Cause obviously I'm not gonna, you know,

01:50:39.600 --> 01:50:41.850
if it's something like that
or the person was doing stuff

01:50:41.850 --> 01:50:42.870
like that, I'd be like, all right,

01:50:42.870 --> 01:50:46.500
this address is probably not
a great address in general.

01:50:46.500 --> 01:50:47.712
- Right, right.
- Yeah.

01:50:47.712 --> 01:50:49.170
But I mean like I'd be
okay finding staying

01:50:49.170 --> 01:50:51.060
there for like temporary or, you know,

01:50:51.060 --> 01:50:53.400
just like, you know, you
stay there and, you know,

01:50:53.400 --> 01:50:54.240
you find out it happens.

01:50:54.240 --> 01:50:55.500
And like that's an interesting story,

01:50:55.500 --> 01:50:58.650
but like there's just
something about settling down

01:50:58.650 --> 01:51:00.210
or just calling somewhere a home

01:51:00.210 --> 01:51:02.100
where something like that has happened

01:51:02.100 --> 01:51:03.740
that would just like,

01:51:03.740 --> 01:51:05.100
it doesn't make me superstitious.

01:51:05.100 --> 01:51:06.900
It's just not a nice thought to have

01:51:06.900 --> 01:51:09.150
where somewhere for a place where you

01:51:09.150 --> 01:51:10.920
should be completely comfortable.

01:51:10.920 --> 01:51:11.826
- Exactly.

01:51:11.826 --> 01:51:12.959
- I guess from my permanent home,

01:51:12.959 --> 01:51:13.980
I might be a bit different towards it.

01:51:13.980 --> 01:51:14.970
- Yeah.
- But towards renting,

01:51:14.970 --> 01:51:16.440
I don't, I couldn't care.

01:51:16.440 --> 01:51:17.273
- Oh yeah, yeah.
- Really?

01:51:17.273 --> 01:51:19.050
- If it's renting and I'm-

01:51:19.050 --> 01:51:20.963
- I wouldn't even be okay
with renting, to be honest.

01:51:20.963 --> 01:51:22.470
- Really?
- Yeah.

01:51:22.470 --> 01:51:24.683
- Even if it's a steal?
- Even if it's a st-

01:51:24.683 --> 01:51:26.460
But there's like there's other ways

01:51:26.460 --> 01:51:27.834
to get a steal, you know.
- Okay, okay.

01:51:27.834 --> 01:51:30.107
- It's just like barter down. (laughing)

01:51:30.107 --> 01:51:35.107
- I did, I'd kill for these
prices, literally. (laughing)

01:51:35.220 --> 01:51:36.924
- I guess, different
question, but when does-

01:51:36.924 --> 01:51:38.698
You move into a new place?

01:51:38.698 --> 01:51:39.531
- [Connor] Okay, okay.

01:51:39.531 --> 01:51:41.993
- When does it start
actually feel like your home

01:51:41.993 --> 01:51:45.450
and not just a place of residence?

01:51:45.450 --> 01:51:47.265
If you've ever felt like that, Connor.

01:51:47.265 --> 01:51:50.160
- The moment you've like

01:51:50.160 --> 01:51:51.927
hit the wall and you've
chipped it and you're like,

01:51:51.927 --> 01:51:55.902
"Oh fuck, fucking hell,
that's my problem. Oh fuck!"

01:51:55.902 --> 01:51:56.795
- What?

01:51:56.795 --> 01:51:58.590
- That's when it hits you.

01:51:58.590 --> 01:51:59.910
- That's literally-

01:51:59.910 --> 01:52:01.138
- I did that day one.

01:52:01.138 --> 01:52:02.600
- Literally day one. (laughing)

01:52:02.600 --> 01:52:03.433
- You are just being irresponsible.

01:52:03.433 --> 01:52:05.040
- Yeah, I did that day
one 'cause I'm like,

01:52:05.040 --> 01:52:06.895
I'm not used to a wall being here.

01:52:06.895 --> 01:52:07.920
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:52:07.920 --> 01:52:09.810
- I chipped a good chunk of like the wood

01:52:09.810 --> 01:52:11.340
in the frame of something
when I was moving

01:52:11.340 --> 01:52:12.173
one of my chairs.

01:52:12.173 --> 01:52:13.297
- [Joey] Right.
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:52:13.297 --> 01:52:14.307
- And I was like, "Oh fuck.

01:52:14.307 --> 01:52:16.980
I'm not gonna get some my
deposit back now. God dammit."

01:52:16.980 --> 01:52:18.990
- It's literally day
one where your furniture

01:52:18.990 --> 01:52:21.180
is just a little bit more heavy

01:52:21.180 --> 01:52:22.980
than you think it's going to be,

01:52:22.980 --> 01:52:25.290
your sofa, you just wanna
move the sofa a little bit.

01:52:25.290 --> 01:52:27.390
And it's just like, you're
just trying to nudge it

01:52:27.390 --> 01:52:29.014
and then it just, (makes ripping noise)

01:52:29.014 --> 01:52:30.300
and it just makes that fucking scratch.

01:52:30.300 --> 01:52:31.133
- Yeah, that scratch.

01:52:31.133 --> 01:52:32.550
- And you never see it coming.

01:52:32.550 --> 01:52:34.140
You're like, I'm going to try my best

01:52:34.140 --> 01:52:35.070
to not make this scratch,

01:52:35.070 --> 01:52:36.900
but it's always like just a little late.

01:52:36.900 --> 01:52:38.670
Like it just slips a little
bit more than you think

01:52:38.670 --> 01:52:39.503
it's going to do.

01:52:39.503 --> 01:52:40.532
- I think-
- And just leave that scratch.

01:52:40.532 --> 01:52:41.365
- I think for me,

01:52:41.365 --> 01:52:43.830
the moment where I know I've
like really settled down

01:52:43.830 --> 01:52:45.930
is when I am a hundred percent aware

01:52:45.930 --> 01:52:47.940
of where everything is in the house.

01:52:47.940 --> 01:52:49.590
Because you have that
period where, you know,

01:52:49.590 --> 01:52:50.700
you're first moving in,

01:52:50.700 --> 01:52:52.878
you're putting shit away in like cabinets

01:52:52.878 --> 01:52:53.727
and, you know, everything.

01:52:53.727 --> 01:52:55.530
And then for a while you're like,

01:52:55.530 --> 01:52:57.060
fuck, where was that thing again?

01:52:57.060 --> 01:52:58.860
And you just like look
all around the house

01:52:58.860 --> 01:52:59.760
because you dunno where it is.

01:52:59.760 --> 01:53:01.320
But the moment where you're
like, (thumb clicking)

01:53:01.320 --> 01:53:03.450
I know exactly where that
really specific thing is.

01:53:03.450 --> 01:53:04.650
I feel that's when it's like.

01:53:04.650 --> 01:53:05.689
- Do you know what it is for me?

01:53:05.689 --> 01:53:06.630
It's really weird for me.

01:53:06.630 --> 01:53:10.350
For me, it's when I can
switch on and off the lights

01:53:10.350 --> 01:53:12.960
without having to look at
them or try to find them,

01:53:12.960 --> 01:53:13.830
you know what I mean?

01:53:13.830 --> 01:53:16.170
Like you move into a new
house and you just like,

01:53:16.170 --> 01:53:17.160
where's the fucking light switch?

01:53:17.160 --> 01:53:18.270
Where's the fucking light switch?

01:53:18.270 --> 01:53:20.872
And then you live there
for like a week or two

01:53:20.872 --> 01:53:22.650
and then you can like
fucking ultra-instinct

01:53:22.650 --> 01:53:23.880
this thing, you know?

01:53:23.880 --> 01:53:25.178
Like what-

01:53:25.178 --> 01:53:26.410
- So, when you enter a room, you just...

01:53:26.410 --> 01:53:27.840
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:53:27.840 --> 01:53:29.670
Right? Especially like
if it's the living room

01:53:29.670 --> 01:53:33.240
and like there's different
switches depending on which part

01:53:33.240 --> 01:53:34.980
of the living room and like you live there

01:53:34.980 --> 01:53:36.690
for long enough, and like, to me,

01:53:36.690 --> 01:53:39.810
